WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.930
In the UK, about 1 in 25 people
carries an allele for cystic fibrosis.

2
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.720
Carriers are healthy.

3
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:12.430
The allele is recessive, so a single
copy causes no illness at all.

4
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.990
You can't pick a carrier out of
a crowd just by looking at them.

5
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:19.520
So how can anyone work out
how many people carry it?

6
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:23.840
In this mission, you'll count alleles
the way population geneticists do:

7
00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.630
copies in a gene pool, not people.

8
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:33.950
Then you'll test real blood group data from
6,129 people against a famous prediction.

9
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.030
Your mission: work out how many
people carry a hidden allele.
